.TH quotadial-daemon 1  "QuotaDial 0.2.0" QuotaDial
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH NAME
quotadial\-daemon \- Run the daemon until Ctrl\-C: the one poller every consumer shares, with history and the local API. While it runs, `status` and `watch` ask it instead of polling
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquotadial daemon\fR [\fB\-\-port\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] 
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run the daemon until Ctrl\-C: the one poller every consumer shares, with history and the local API. While it runs, `status` and `watch` ask it instead of polling
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-port\fR \fI<PORT>\fR [default: 47115]
The port for the local API, on 127.0.0.1. 0 lets the system choose a free one
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.SH "SEE ALSO"
quotadial(1). The full guide is docs/CLI.md in QuotaDial\*(Aqs repository, https://github.com/pghmatt/quotadial, and quotadial.com.
